        "original_id": "a4a8d9c0-6965-54d8-9f30-9b891878b8a4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Aubrey Otis Hampton\n- Organizations: Massachusetts General Hospital, Walter Reed Army Medical Center, Walter Reed General Hospital, U.S. Army\n- Places: Copeville, Texas, Washington, D.C.\n- Roles: Radiologist, Chief of Radiology\n- Concepts: Hampton's hump, Hampton's line\n\nFacts:\n- Aubrey Otis Hampton was born in 1900 in Copeville, Texas, and he died in 1955.\n- Walter Reed Army Medical Center was the U.S. Army's flagship medical center from 1909 to 2011.\n- Walter Reed Army Medical Center was known as Walter Reed General Hospital until 1951.\n- Aubrey Otis Hampton was an American radiologist remembered for describing Hampton's hump and Hampton's line.\n- Aubrey Otis Hampton became chief of radiology at Massachusetts General Hospital in 1941.\n- Aubrey Otis Hampton served as chief of radiology at Walter Reed Army Hospital in Washington, D.C. from 1942 to 1945.",
